  "about": "The characters a tool-approval surface shows as <U+XXXX> instead of themselves: Unicode's Cc, Cf and Default_Ignorable_Code_Point (16.0) plus U+2028 and U+2029, less \\n and \\t, which the pretty-printed arguments' own layout uses. Inclusive ranges of hex code points, sorted and disjoint. A one-line field (a tool name, an agent id) has no layout of its own, so it also shows line_adds escaped: every White_Space character but the plain space U+0020 (\\t, \\n, the no-break, Ogham, en to hair, narrow no-break, math and ideographic spaces) and U+2800 BRAILLE PATTERN BLANK, as ranges of the same shape, outside ranges. Its set is ranges plus line_adds, and line_cases are worked cases of it. One table for two languages: the Rust side (openalpaca_core::utils::text::needs_escape, escape_hidden, hidden_notice, needs_escape_in_line, escape_hidden_line) is held equal to every range, case and notice here by a test that reads this file; the GUI derives its set from it. Change both sides together.",
